@brian_spiegel - You say "persuasive article", but what I'd like to see from GPT is a well written and reasonably fair article presenting both sides clearly and without bias. In other words, not a piece of pro-Turkish propaganda; rather, an intellectual deep dive into the reasons why this particular historical issue is (relatively) poorly documented and how estimates of the death toll are inherently problematic and probably highly political.

@jesseshum - The way to get something that's not pro something is to give it a task that starts by asking it to present both arguments neutrally and even-handedly. I am not familiar with what is in GPT about the Armenian Genocide, but if you want its take on that, then you need to give it a task to present both arguments neutrally and even-handedly.

